  https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/fundamentals/package-validation/diagnostic-ids

  Every entry here is a deliberate, reviewed decision. A suppression that nobody can explain is a
  silenced bug, so do not add one without recording why below, and delete one the moment the reason
  stops holding. Regenerating this file with -p:ApiCompatGenerateSuppressionFile=true rewrites it and
  DISCARDS these comments - regenerate into a scratch copy and merge by hand instead.

  Bodu.Core's DayOfWeekSet replaces WeekPattern in 1.3.0, and every Calendar API that took or
  returned a WeekPattern now takes or returns a DayOfWeekSet (CP0002 for each): the workingWeek
  parameter of the working-day and fiscal extensions, ResolutionPolicy's constructor and WorkingWeek
  property, and AdjustmentPolicy.IsTriggered and ApplyAction. This is a deliberate break inside a
  minor release, chosen for 1.3.0 and called out in its release notes. Stored data is unchanged:
  documents keep workingDays="0111110", and .bcal packs keep Sunday at bit 6. Delete these entries
  when the Stable validation baseline moves to 1.3.0.
-->
